body:
This issue should not be closed, I still have it in the latest canary version in my local project.

And I also encounter it in 13.3.4.

```
error - TypeError: Cannot set properties of undefined (setting 'current')
    at prepareHostDispatcher (C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\compiled\react-dom\cjs\react-dom-server.edge.development.js:1896:37)
    at createRequest (C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\compiled\react-dom\cjs\react-dom-server.edge.development.js:8299:3)
    at C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\compiled\react-dom\cjs\react-dom-server.edge.development.js:10126:19
    at new Promise (<anonymous>)
    at Object.renderToReadableStream (C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\compiled\react-dom\cjs\react-dom-server.edge.development.js:10092:10)  
    at C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\server\node-web-streams-helper.js:195:117
    at NextTracerImpl.trace (C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\server\lib\trace\tracer.js:86:20)
    at renderToInitialStream (C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\server\node-web-streams-helper.js:195:37)
    at C:\Users\picheva1\workspace\iv4\node_modules\next\dist\server\app-render\app-render.js:937:92
    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:95:5) {
  page: '/'
}
```

In `\node_modules\next\dist\compiled\react-dom\cjs\react-dom-server.edge.development.js` , I can see this code

```js
var ReactDOMSharedInternals = ReactDOM.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED;

var ReactDOMCurrentDispatcher = ReactDOMSharedInternals.Dispatcher;
var ReactDOMServerDispatcher = {
  prefetchDNS: prefetchDNS,
  preconnect: preconnect,
  preload: preload,
  preinit: preinit
};
function prepareHostDispatcher() {
  ReactDOMCurrentDispatcher.current = ReactDOMServerDispatcher;
} // Used to distinguish these contexts from ones used in other renderers.
```

ergo: `ReactDOM.__SECRET_INTERNALS_DO_NOT_USE_OR_YOU_WILL_BE_FIRED.Dispatcher` is null.

So, should `var ReactDOM = require('react-dom')` not import from `node_modules/react-dom` ?
